/-!
# A normal branch of a normal crossings divisor is regular

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring with a strict henselization `A^{sh}`, and suppose
`A^{sh}` is a regular local ring. Let `y ∈ 𝔪` be an element whose quotient `A / (y)` is a normal
domain, and suppose the image of `y` in `A^{sh}` divides the product `h₁ ⋯ h_s` of an initial
segment of a regular system of parameters `h₁, …, h_d` of `A^{sh}`. Then `A / (y)` is a regular
local ring.

Geometrically, `y` cuts out one branch of a normal crossings divisor; the hypothesis is that the
branch is normal at the point, and the conclusion is that it is in fact regular there. This is
the step of Stacks 0CBS that upgrades normality to regularity, and the reason the local structure
of a normal crossings divisor can be read off one factor at a time.

## Main results

* `isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_dvd_prod`: the statement above, with
  normality of `A / (y)` taken apart as `IsDomain` together with `IsIntegrallyClosed`.
* `isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_isNormalRing_of_dvd_prod`: the same with normality packaged as
  `IsNormalRing`.

## Implementation notes

Everything happens in `A^{sh}`, where unique factorization is available. The quotient
`A^{sh} / y A^{sh}` is a strict henselization of `A / (y)` by Stacks 05WS, so normality ascends
to it by Stacks 06DI and regularity descends from it by Stacks 06LN. Normality of
`A^{sh} / y A^{sh}` says exactly that the image `y'` of `y` generates a prime ideal, and `y'` is
nonzero because it divides a product of regular parameters, each of which is a prime element of
the regular local ring `A^{sh}`. A prime dividing a list product divides one entry, and two
primes that divide one another are associated, so `y' A^{sh} = h A^{sh}` for a single entry `h`
of the regular system of parameters. The quotient by one such entry is regular, which is the
content of
`IsRegularLocalRing.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_of_mem_isSystemOfParameters`.

A strict henselization is `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization A L Ash` for a separably closed extension
`L` of the residue field of `A`, so `IsSepClosure (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) L` is carried as a
separate instance. Regularity of `Ash` is an instance rather than a hypothesis, which also
supplies its localness and Noetherianity. Sequences are `List`s, as in
`IsLocalRing.IsSystemOfParameters`, and the ideal generated by a list is `Ideal.ofList`; a
*regular* system of parameters is the conjunction of `IsLocalRing.IsSystemOfParameters` with
`Ideal.ofList hs = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Ash`, so both conjuncts are carried explicitly.

Stacks 05WS returns the defining properties of a strict henselization of `A / I` as a package
rather than as an `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization` instance, so the instance is rebuilt from it by
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.of_ind_etale`, taking the residue field of `A^{sh} / I A^{sh}`
itself as the prescribed residue extension, for which the required residue field identification
is the identity. Applying Stacks 05WS also needs the separable closedness of the actual residue
field of `A^{sh}` rather than of the prescribed `L`, which is
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.exists_residueFieldAlgebra` once the algebra structure it produces
is identified with the canonical one. Both Stacks 06DI and Stacks 06LN compare a ring
simultaneously with a henselization and with a strict henselization, so an auxiliary plain
henselization is produced by Stacks 04GN
(`IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_residueField`) and immediately discarded. The two transfers
are packaged into a single auxiliary statement because they share that whole setup.

## References

* [StacksProject 0CBS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBS), the local structure of a
  normal crossings divisor
* [StacksProject 06DI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06DI), normality is unchanged by a
  (strict) henselization
* [StacksProject 06LN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06LN), regularity is unchanged by a
  (strict) henselization
* [StacksProject 05WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05WS), strict henselization is
  compatible with quotients
* [StacksProject 04GN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04GN), existence of a henselization
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

universe u v

/-- **Normality ascends to, and regularity descends from, the quotient of a strict
henselization.** Let `Ash` be a strict henselization of a Noetherian local ring `(A, 𝔪)` and let
`I ⊆ 𝔪` be an ideal. Then `Ash / I Ash` is a strict henselization of `A / I`, so normality of
`A / I` makes `Ash / I Ash` a domain, and regularity of `Ash / I Ash` makes `A / I` regular. -/
@[ega "IV 18.8.13" "(c)"]
private theorem transfer_quotient_of_isHenselization
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {Ash : Type u} [CommRing Ash] [IsLocalRing Ash] [Algebra A Ash]
    (L : Type v) [Field L] [Algebra (ResidueField A) L] [IsSepClosure (ResidueField A) L]
    [IsHenselization A L Ash] (I : Ideal A) (hI : I ≤ maximalIdeal A) :
    (IsDomain (A ⧸ I) → IsIntegrallyClosed (A ⧸ I) →
        IsDomain (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash))) ∧
      (IsRegularLocalRing (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)) → IsRegularLocalRing (A ⧸ I)) := by
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A Ash) := IsHenselization.isLocalHom (L := L)
  have : HenselianLocalRing Ash := IsHenselization.henselian (R := A) (L := L)
  -- Replace the prescribed residue extension `L` by the actual residue field of `Ash`.
  obtain ⟨a, _, hsep, hres⟩ :=
    IsHenselization.exists_residueFieldAlgebra (R := A) (L := L) (Rh := Ash)
  have halg : a = ResidueField.instAlgebra (R := A) (S := Ash) :=
    Algebra.algebra_ext _ _ <| residue_surjective.forall.2 fun r ↦
      (hres r).trans (ResidueField.algebraMap_residue (S := Ash) r).symm
  subst halg
  have : IsSepClosure (ResidueField A) (ResidueField Ash) := hsep inferInstance
  -- Stacks 05WS: the quotient of `Ash` is a strict henselization of the quotient of `A`.
  obtain ⟨hlocQ, hlocAQ, _, hhens, hind, _, hsepQ⟩ :=
    IsLocalRing.strictHenselization_quotient (R := A) (Rsh := Ash)
      (IsHenselization.ind_etale_of_universe_le.{u, v, u} L)
      (IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal (R := A) (L := L) (Rh := Ash)) I hI
  have := hlocQ
  have := hlocAQ
  have := hsepQ
  have : IsHenselization (A ⧸ I) (ResidueField (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)))
      (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)) :=
    IsHenselization.of_ind_etale hhens hind
      ⟨RingEquiv.refl _, fun z ↦ ResidueField.algebraMap_residue z⟩
  -- Both Stacks 06DI and Stacks 06LN want a plain henselization of `A / I` as well.
  obtain ⟨Ah, _, _, _, _⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_residueField (A ⧸ I)
  have htfae := isNormalDomain_tfae_henselization_strictHenselization (A ⧸ I) Ah
    (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)) (ResidueField (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)))
  have h13 : (IsDomain (A ⧸ I) ∧ IsIntegrallyClosed (A ⧸ I)) ↔
      (IsDomain (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)) ∧
        IsIntegrallyClosed (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash))) := htfae.out 1 3
  refine ⟨fun hdom hic ↦ (h13.mp ⟨hdom, hic⟩).1, fun hreg ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact (isRegularLocalRing_iff_henselizations (A ⧸ I) Ah
      (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash))
      (ResidueField (Ash ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A Ash)))).2.mpr hreg

/-- **A normal branch of a normal crossings divisor is regular.** Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian
local ring, let `Ash` be a strict henselization of `A` relative to a separably closed extension
`L` of the residue field of `A`, and suppose `Ash` is a regular local ring. Let `y ∈ 𝔪` be an
element such that `A / (y)` is a normal domain, and let `h₁, …, h_d` be a regular system of
parameters of `Ash`. If the image of `y` in `Ash` divides the product `h₁ ⋯ h_s` of an initial
segment, then `A / (y)` is a regular local ring. -/
public theorem isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_dvd_prod
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {Ash : Type u} [CommRing Ash] [IsRegularLocalRing Ash] [Algebra A Ash]
    (L : Type u) [Field L] [Algebra (ResidueField A) L]
    [IsSepClosure (ResidueField A) L] [IsHenselization A L Ash]
    {y : A} (hy : y ∈ maximalIdeal A)
    (hdom : IsDomain (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}))
    (hic : IsIntegrallyClosed (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}))
    {hs : List Ash} {s : ℕ} (hsop : IsSystemOfParameters hs)
    (hsgen : Ideal.ofList hs = maximalIdeal Ash) (_hsle : s ≤ hs.length)
    (hdvd : algebraMap A Ash y ∣ (hs.take s).prod) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}) := by
  have : IsDomain Ash := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain Ash
  -- A regular system of parameters is a minimal generating sequence of the maximal ideal.
  have hlen : hs.length = (maximalIdeal Ash).spanFinrank := by
    have hdim := IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := Ash)
    rw [hsop.2] at hdim
    exact_mod_cast hdim.symm
  -- Hence every entry is a prime element, and the truncated product is nonzero.
  have hprime : ∀ h ∈ hs, Prime h := fun h hh ↦
    IsRegularLocalRing.prime_of_mem_of_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal hsgen hlen hh
  have hsub : hs.take s ⊆ hs := List.take_subset s hs
  have hprod : (hs.take s).prod ≠ 0 :=
    List.prod_ne_zero fun h0 ↦ (hprime 0 (hsub h0)).ne_zero rfl
  have hy0 : algebraMap A Ash y ≠ 0 := fun h0 ↦ hprod (zero_dvd_iff.mp (h0 ▸ hdvd))
  -- Transfer along the strict henselization `Ash / y Ash` of `A / (y)`.
  have hmap : (Ideal.span {y}).map (algebraMap A Ash) = Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ash y} := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  obtain ⟨hup, hdown⟩ := transfer_quotient_of_isHenselization (A := A) (Ash := Ash) L
    (Ideal.span {y}) (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hy))
  have hdomq : IsDomain (Ash ⧸ Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ash y}) := hmap ▸ hup hdom hic
  -- Normality of the quotient means the image of `y` is a prime element of `Ash`.
  have hyprime : Prime (algebraMap A Ash y) :=
    (Ideal.span_singleton_prime hy0).mp ((Ideal.Quotient.isDomain_iff_prime _).mp hdomq)
  -- A prime dividing the product divides one entry, and is then associated to it.
  obtain ⟨h, hmem, hhdvd⟩ := hyprime.dvd_prod_iff.mp hdvd
  have hspan : Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ash y} = Ideal.span {h} :=
    Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton.mpr
      (hyprime.associated_of_dvd (hprime h (hsub hmem)) hhdvd)
  -- The quotient by one entry of a regular system of parameters is regular.
  refine hdown ?_
  rw [hmap, hspan]
  exact IsRegularLocalRing.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_of_mem_isSystemOfParameters
    hsop hsgen (hsub hmem)

/-- **A normal branch of a normal crossings divisor is regular**, with normality of `A / (y)`
given as `IsNormalRing`. See
`isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_dvd_prod`. -/
public theorem isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_isNormalRing_of_dvd_prod
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {Ash : Type u} [CommRing Ash] [IsRegularLocalRing Ash] [Algebra A Ash]
    (L : Type u) [Field L] [Algebra (ResidueField A) L]
    [IsSepClosure (ResidueField A) L] [IsHenselization A L Ash]
    {y : A} (hy : y ∈ maximalIdeal A) (hnor : IsNormalRing (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}))
    {hs : List Ash} {s : ℕ} (hsop : IsSystemOfParameters hs)
    (hsgen : Ideal.ofList hs = maximalIdeal Ash) (hsle : s ≤ hs.length)
    (hdvd : algebraMap A Ash y ∣ (hs.take s).prod) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}) := by
  have hne : Ideal.span {y} ≠ ⊤ := ne_top_of_le_ne_top (maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).ne_top
    (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hy))
  have : Nontrivial (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
  have : IsLocalRing (A ⧸ Ideal.span {y}) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  obtain ⟨hdom, hic⟩ := hnor.of_isLocalRing
  exact isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_dvd_prod L hy hdom hic hsop hsgen
    hsle hdvd

end
